# Deployment

## Mục tiêu

Deployment là quá trình đưa code từ development environment đến production, nơi users có thể interact với nó. Một deployment strategy tốt đảm bảo rằng changes được delivered safely, reliably, và with minimal disruption. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, deployment không chỉ là "push code" mà là một structured process bao gồm infrastructure provisioning, configuration management, security hardening, và operational readiness.

Mục tiêu là enable frequent, reliable deployments with confidence. Teams nên có thể deploy multiple times per day without fear. Điều này đòi hỏi automation, proper testing, good monitoring, và well-defined rollback procedures.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Automate Everything**

Manual deployments are error-prone. Automate the entire deployment pipeline. From code commit to production. Infrastructure as code. Configuration as code. Scripts should be version controlled.

**2. Infrastructure as Code**

Define infrastructure in code. Use Terraform, Pulumi, or CloudFormation. Version control infrastructure. Review infrastructure changes. Environments should be identical. Reproducible infrastructure.

**3. Immutable Infrastructure**

Never modify running servers. Deploy new instances with new code. Destroy old instances. Immutable deployments reduce drift. Easier rollbacks. Consistent environments.

**4. Blue-Green Deployments**

Run two identical environments. Blue is current production. Green is new version. Switch traffic when green is ready. Instant rollback by switching back. Zero downtime deployments possible.

**5. Canary Releases**

Deploy to small subset of users first. Monitor for issues. Gradually increase traffic. Roll back if problems detected. Reduces blast radius. Data-driven release decisions.

**6. Feature Flags**

Decouple deployment from release. Deploy code that's disabled. Enable features gradually. Instant kill switch. A/B testing capability. Emergency disable.

**7. Zero Downtime Deployments**

Design for continuous availability. Use rolling updates. Health checks before traffic switch. Load balancer integration. Handle in-flight requests. Never force kill requests.

**8. Rollback Ready**

Always have rollback plan. Test rollback procedures. Keep previous versions deployable. Database migrations must be reversible. Document rollback steps. Practice rollbacks regularly.

**9. Environment Parity**

Development should mirror production. Use same infrastructure. Same configurations. Same versions. Local development vs production parity. Reduces "works on my machine" issues.

**10. Deployment Verification**

Verify deployments automatically. Health checks. Smoke tests. Synthetic monitoring. Alert on deployment failures. Automated rollback on failure.

