## Anti Pattern

**1. Manual Deployments**

Deploying manually by logging into servers. Error-prone process. Not repeatable. No audit trail. No easy rollback. Leads to "works on my machine" issues.

**2. Big Bang Releases**

Deploying many changes at once. Hard to identify cause of issues. Long development cycles. Difficult rollback. High risk. Instead, deploy small changes frequently.

**3. No Testing Before Production**

Deploying without proper testing. Only testing in production. Users discover bugs. Reputation damage. Test thoroughly before deployment.

**4. Configuration Drift**

Different configurations across environments. Subtle bugs appear. Hard to reproduce issues. Configuration management is essential.

**5. Long-Lived Branches**

Feature branches that live for weeks. Merge hell at release time. Integrate frequently. Use trunk-based development.

